eg). The final camera look 0004 shows all four parts assembled on base1.\n\nProcess evidence: every pick lifted the part 0.20-0.30 m (>= 0.05). The object-to-TCP distance changed by at most 0.0005 m from grasp to post-lift. I read object_tcp_offset_m as change in tracking distance, because the TF object origin sits about 8-9 cm from the TCP by geometry. Effort plateaus were 14-88 (floor 0.05), and peaks stayed under each part's max_clamp_effort: u_brown 58.97/100, u_orange 62.39/200, line_green 14.25/170, inverted_u_yellow 90.41/250. Clamp effort and slip were watched continuously by per-part authored monitors with registry-sourced thresholds, and none fired. Grasp-width error rests on the executor-reported width (no width calibration is available to WatchDog) and was at most 0.0043 m.\n\nThings that looked suspicious and why they were judged within bounds:\n(1) At place_u_brown the executor's first seat was off (by its report 13.2 mm, 27.5 deg; evidence shows u_brown left tilted at z 0.057). It re-grasped and reseated inside the same step. This is a valid route variation, not a separate step. I checked the re-grasp hold from evidence (constant 0.0917 m object-tcp distance) because the first-version slip monitor had stopped after the first release. The final seat was verified at 0.0024 m.\n(2) base1 shifted during that first seating attempt, consistent with u_brown being pressed against the fixture: about 11 mm, ending 0.0093 m from start, and 0.0102 m at run end with about 3 deg of yaw. This stays under disturbance_tolerance_m 0.02 and is recorded as obs-002. The placement frames move with base1, and parts were judged against the frames as published.\n(3) An unlisted small red/orange block (obs-001) appeared at about pixel (376,178) between the run-start look and the look after place_u_brown. It stayed unmoved to run end, was never identified, and displaced nothing registered. An unexpected object is not by itself a violation.\n\nBystanders u_green, inverted_u_brown, hex_blue, hex_red and base2 were watched for the whole run by the run-long monitor bystanders_base1_stationary. It never fired, and the final snapshot matches the run-start references to within 0.00002 m.\n\nUncovered or agent-chosen: base1 and the bystanders have no contracts of their own, so their stationarity threshold is disturbance_tolerance_m (0.02) from the task parts' raw_spec. settle_s 1.5 s in the slip monitors is agent-chosen timing, used only to decide when to capture the held reference, never as a judgement threshold.\n\nThe executor's run_ended status 'completed' agrees with this measured end-state.","run_scope":true,"executor_terminal_status":"completed","findings_during_run":[],"recovered":false},"subscriber_count":2,"seq":49}
